Description: Keep a screencopy renderer per capture size
 BasicScreenShooter kept one Renderer, for the size of the last capture.
 grim and similar wlr-screencopy clients capture each output in turn, so
 with two monitors of different sizes every screenshot built two new GL
 renderers (shader compiles, blur targets) and threw them away again. The
 Umoja overview refreshes its window previews this way in the background,
 which rebuilt a pair of renderers every 10 seconds. Keep up to four, one
 per size, most recently used first.
Author: Umoja
Forwarded: no

